Gross! Brad: It will help hold the pieces

16
00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:45.443
together. Danny: How about this rubber

17
00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.065
band? Brad: That will be

18
00:00:47.066 --> 00:00:49.734
good. We need something

19
00:00:49.735 --> 00:00:53.000
more. Danny: I found some string and a popsicle

20
00:00:53.001 --> 00:00:54.884
stick. Will that

21
00:00:54.885 --> 00:01:04.539
help? Brad: Sure. It's worth a try.

22
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.008
Ta-da! Danny: I don't think it's going to

23
00:01:07.009 --> 00:01:08.549
work. Brad: Don't say

24
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.974
that. I haven't tried it

25
00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:14.614
yet. Danny: Okay. Give it a

26
00:01:14.615 --> 00:01:19.835
try. Brad: I think the bullies were standing

27
00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:22.075
here. Danny: Nothing is

28
00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:23.858
happening. Brad: I see

29
00:01:23.859 --> 00:01:26.049
that. Danny: Brad, we're both

30
00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.606
wet. We don't have any more

31
00:01:28.607 --> 00:01:31.629
nano-putty. There's nothing more we can do!

32
00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.375
Brad: Maybe, if I had a paper clip or something metallic . . .

33
00:01:36.376 --> 00:01:40.109
Danny: Don't you ever give up?

34
00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.084
Brad: I see a gum wrapper.

35
00:01:43.085 --> 00:01:45.289
